.SH VMDK SESSIONS
The vmdk mode uses the DynBlk driver with standard split sparse VMDK storage.
Managed sessions contain volume.vmdk and its volume-sNNN.vmdk extents.
Compression is unavailable. The default size is 16384 MiB; installed limits are
queried per format. The running initrd must advertise vmdk-session-v1.
Creation, resize, copy, clone, conversion and logical export/import support vmdk.
.SH SPACE RECLAMATION
.B minios-session reclaim ID [--compact] [--json]
.PP
Trim the unencrypted internal ext4 and reclaim known free container space
for DynFileFS, DynBlk or VMDK sessions.
The running device is validated against this boot and remains connected.
Inactive sessions are temporarily attached and mounted.
Only --compact permits live-data relocation; it is never an automatic fallback
on exFAT. Compaction increases flash writes. Encrypted sessions reclaim only
already-known free storage and do not enable discard through LUKS.
The GUI provides the same operation as Free Space in the session context menu.
.PP
DynFileFS requires version 4.6.0 or later. Running sessions are supported by
exposing the hidden FUSE image inside a private mount namespace; the working
session's mounts and loop device remain connected in the original namespace.
The actual running daemon is checked before trimming. If an older daemon is
still running after a package update, reboot with the updated backend first.
The displayed DynFileFS usage reflects allocated blocks, including hole punching.
